# EXCALIBUR — environment (all optional)
#
# Credentials
# -----------
# EXCALIBUR runs on whatever Claude credential your environment already provides.
# Set ONE of the following (or none, to use a Claude subscription via
# `claude setup-token`). Run `python tools/auth_preflight.py` to see which one is
# detected and whether it works.
#
#   Anthropic API key
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
#   LLM gateway (LiteLLM, Portkey, your org's proxy, ...)
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://llm-gateway.example.com
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=your-gateway-token
#
#   Amazon Bedrock  (plus the usual AWS_* credentials)
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1
#
#   Google Cloud  (plus gcloud application-default credentials)
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=1
# CLOUD_ML_REGION=us-east5
#
#   Microsoft Foundry
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY=1
#
#   Claude Platform on AWS
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_ANTHROPIC_AWS=1
# ANTHROPIC_AWS_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...

# Model
# -----
# Leave unset to use your provider's default. Set it to pin a specific model —
# note the correct form differs per provider: a model id on the Anthropic API,
# an inference profile ARN on Bedrock, a version name on Google Cloud, a
# deployment name on Foundry.
# EXCALIBUR_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7

# Reasoning controls. Not every model accepts these — Haiku 4.5 and older models
# reject `effort`, and most gateway shims reject `thinking`. Set either to `none`
# to omit it from the request, which is what makes cheap and proxied models work.
# EXCALIBUR_EFFORT=high        # low | medium | high | xhigh | max | none
# EXCALIBUR_THINKING=adaptive  # adaptive | none

# App
# ---
# Port for the web server (default 4500)
# PORT=4500

# Override where project JSON files are stored (default ./projects)
# PROJECTS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/projects
